-- The 22 borrowers, and THIS BLOCK IS DELIBERATELY ORDER-INDEPENDENT.
--
-- `legal_entity` is shared with cp-00 and cp-01, and the three fixtures declare it
-- THREE DIFFERENT WAYS — cp-00's has `source` and a primary key, cp-01's has neither.
-- Every `create table` is `if not exists`, so WHICHEVER MODULE RUNS FIRST WINS and the
-- surviving column set depends on collection order. Naming a column the other
-- definition lacks fails the whole insert; relying on a primary key the other lacks
-- silently duplicates rows and turns this product's borrower join into a fan-out.
--
-- So: only the 5 columns ALL THREE definitions share, and a DELETE of exactly
-- these LEIs first. cp-02 then owns these rows outright, in any order, with or without
-- a unique index. The rows are identical to what the other fixtures would have loaded —
-- the same estate — so deleting and reinserting them changes nothing for those modules.
--
-- AVIS BUDGET GROUP is cp-01's own demonstration anchor and this product's
-- inverted-date-pair borrower, so the overlap is real and cannot be engineered away.
on conflict (lei) do nothing;

-- 14 reconciliation rows, covering 14 of the 22 borrowers. ONE carries
-- `plausible = false` and it is the live negative instance `S` needs.

-- The 4 principals — shared with cp-01, same delete-then-insert reasoning.
